    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0454" n="338" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg338"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.00/829a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Smith.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 9, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>All reports from Haiti indicate that Zamor Government will probably be stable and
                    able to preserve order, but the President prefers to delay recognition until
                    situation is more settled.</p>
                <p>Please inquire of Government what guaranties it can give as to its permanence and
                    ability to protect lives and property of foreigners. Also report how many
                    provinces have accepted the new President and how many are in revolt.</p>
                <p>What is the attitude of Davilmar Theodore and what prospect is there of his being
                    able to disturb the new Government?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
